	<!-- The roof (the stakes rework; built as in Towns since 2026-10-31):
	     the order goes on the level the player marks from above the walls,
	     or on top of the walls when the hall itself is marked
	     (Task.getRoofLevel).  The crew lays it from its own level, the top
	     of a ladder, then from the roof already laid, never from the hall
	     below (Task.getPlacingPoints); a job waits until someone can reach
	     it (TaskManager, Task.hasRoofAccess).  Base, as Towns' floors: the
	     crew walks on it to lay the rest.  It never falls (dcRoof,
	     Item.shouldFall) and keeps the rain off (Weather); wall makes it
	     cast Towns' sun shadow, so the hall under it shows shaded -->
	<dcroof>
		<name>Roof</name>
		<description>Keeps the rain off what is under it. Your crew needs a ladder up to the roof: they lay it from there and walk on it.</description>
		<canBeBuiltOnHoles>true</canBeBuiltOnHoles>
		<wall>true</wall>
		<base>true</base>
		<!-- Operative even loose: a dropped piece showed Towns' red cross (not installed) and could not be carried back into place -->
		<alwaysOperative>true</alwaysOperative>
		<dcRoof>1</dcRoof>
		<value>1</value>
	</dcroof>

